+**The loop is bounded** (`supervisor.md`, Phase 2): at most four rounds per subject, a non-convergent finding starting none; then, if the text changed after a critic last read it, one confirming read by both, whose file opens by saying so and holds the diff since each critic's last read, labelled by critic, and which no critique round follows; then one resolution round, `DESIGN-<subject>-R1.md`, holding every question still Blocking or non-convergent, whose file opens with *answer every open question in this file; raise no new finding; your reply answers each question in place of findings, with no counts*, and whose Review B reply the supervisor writes to `run/review/REVIEW-DESIGN-<subject>-R<n>.md` for `plan-critic`; then the gate, whatever is still open. A subject is one token of lower-case letters, digits and hyphens, distinct from every other subject. A failed launch follows the supervisor's step 3b, every one recorded: the first (exit 4) runs once more on the same file, the second (exit 3) marks the model and runs once on the re-resolved profile; then the design waits for the roster or the owner's word, and the file runs once more under its number with no re-runs; if that fails too, the round stays not run and the subject goes on to its resolution round or its gate. `bridge-run.py` refuses, with exit 125 and a message beginning `bridge-run: refused - design ceiling: `, a `cursor-agent` launch naming, anywhere and with either separator, a `run/review/DESIGN-<name>.md` whose round (the name's last hyphen-separated part: a positive integer without a leading zero, or `R` and one; 1 to 5 and `R1` allowed) is above five, is `R2` or later, or cannot be read, a name holding anything but lower-case letters, digits, hyphens and the round's `R` being one that cannot. A line `Design rounds above five: <subject> <rounds> (<their words>, <date>)` in `docs/RUN_PARAMETERS.md`, written only on the owner's own words, allows that subject rounds up to `<rounds>` and `R2`, and nothing beyond: the same shape once more, critique rounds up to `<rounds>` minus one, a confirming read at `<rounds>` at the most, then the next resolution round if anything is open. `<rounds>` is a round number: the last numbered round run, a resolution round not counted, plus the more rounds the owner names, or five more when they name none, never below six; a subject is lifted once, its first well-formed line standing and a later one ignored. A refusal is neither a failed review nor a model's failure. The convergence rule of the code gate does not apply to a design critique.
 
